  "summary": "Bind normal Queue Run Once to an authoritative backend dry-run and require the active PowerShell discovery plan to match before media dispatch.",
  "reason": "Queue snapshots lacked durable input/plan provenance, blank Run Once treated stale or mismatched evidence as advisory, pending-publish classification could diverge, and pipeline.start command evidence reported completion immediately after spawn.",
  "affected_areas": [
    "backend",
    "desktop-api",
    "docs",
    "documentation",
    "generated-context",
    "local-api",
    "pending-publish",
    "pipeline",
    "powershell-engine",
    "process-lifecycle",
    "queue",
    "tests",
    "webview"
  ],
  "behavior_before": "Queue dry-run snapshots could be displayed or launched without request/input/plan parity proof; queue policy writes refreshed the cached payload without rebuilding backend curation; active discovery did not compare itself to the accepted preview; accepted pipeline starts were journaled as completed at spawn time.",
  "behavior_after": "Queue scan uses request-unique temporary output, stable input fingerprints, atomic promotion, explicit cached-fallback evidence, pending-index health, and a full uncapped plan fingerprint. Blank Run Once requires current matching evidence inside the durable lease, passes the accepted fingerprint to PowerShell, and exits blocked before media dispatch on disagreement. Queue policy writes request a new scan, and command evidence progresses through accepted/running/rejected to observer-recorded terminal outcomes.",
